            "text": "Decoder memory safety — attacker-controlled length driving memcpy — Requires further review: src/mqtt.c unpack_mqtt_connect (ClientId copy, will/username/password)\n\nCONFIRMED BY TRACE, needs dynamic reproduction. mqtt.c:240 memcpy(client_id, buf, cid_len) with cid_len a raw u16 from the wire into u8 client_id[64] (mqtt.h:181) that lives in the stack-resident io.data (server.c:860). No bounds check anywhere; `len` param unused. PoC bytes recorded in note 5243eb (303-byte CONNECT, cid_len=0x0100). Nearest case: ASAN stack-buffer-overflow WRITE; production: stack smashing/control-flow overwrite. Highest-value candidate on target.</evidence>"
