          "message": {
            "text": "Decoder primitives — allocation/copy helpers and their failure modes — Ruled out: src/pack.c unpack / unpack_bytes / unpack_string16 / unpack_integer\n\nruled_out as a memory-safety issue with the named control: unpack_bytes (pack.c:411-418) can never return NULL because try_alloc (memory.c:46-57) either returns a valid pointer or calls exit(EXIT_FAILURE) — so the four `if (!ptr) return -MQTT_ERR` guards (mqtt.c:301,318,352,397) and the `err:` labels (mqtt.c:365,408) are dead code, i.e. the partial-decode leak path cannot happen. No bounds parameter exists, which is why the *callers* are the findings (notes 5243eb/1cc769/1076b3). unpack_integer/unpackiXX read fixed widths with no bounds (1/2/4/8 bytes) — safe only relative to the 512KB rbuf, see D8."
          },
