          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Consumption of decoded topic/payload fields (VLA sizing, wbuf writes, retained store) — Requires further review: src/handlers.c publish_handler + publish_message\n\nCONFIRMED BY TRACE. handlers.c:696-706: `char topic[p->topiclen+2]` VLA then `p->topic[p->topiclen-1]` -> index -1 when topiclen==0 (heap read inside the try_alloc size header, ASAN-invisible); handlers.c:746-749 stores a full serialized copy of the attacker PUBLISH as the retained message, which is the primitive for the wbuf overflow. Payload bytes / payloadlen reach pack_mqtt_publish (mqtt.c:520) via publish_message (handlers.c:227). See note 99b93f (D11) and 392a40-adjacent D10 note."
