          "message": {
            "text": "Consumption of decoded tuple fields (VLA sizing, index underflow, wbuf write) — Requires further review: src/handlers.c subscribe_handler (rcs/topic VLAs, retained-message copy)\n\nCONFIRMED BY TRACE. handlers.c:545 `unsigned char rcs[s->tuples_len]` and handlers.c:557-569 `char topic[topic_len+2]` are attacker-sized VLAs (up to 64KB each, ~128KB of stack per handler call) and handlers.c:563/564 index topic[-1]/[-2] when topic_len is 0 or 1 (stack-buffer-underflow READ, 7-byte PoC `82 05 00 01 00 00 02`, note 392a40). handlers.c:615-619 copies each topic's retained message into c->wbuf + c->towrite with no boundary check, once per tuple including duplicates, giving a controlled heap overflow on the 512KB wbuf and a subsequent heap read-back through send_data (note 99b93f)."
