            "text": "Consumption of decoded CONNECT fields (client id, credentials, LWT) — No issue identified: src/handlers.c connect_handler + set_connack + check_passwd\n\nReviewed handlers.c:345-495. The decoded ClientId is only consumed through bounds-limited calls once the overflow in the decoder (note 5243eb) has not already fired: snprintf(cc->client_id, MQTT_CLIENT_ID_LEN, \"%s\", ...) at :394 and generate_random_id's snprintf(dest, MQTT_CLIENT_ID_LEN-1, ...) at util.c:139. Auth path (allow_anonymous=false) looks up the NUL-terminated username via uthash and calls check_passwd -> crypt(passwd, salt) + STREQ with strlen(salt) (util.c:142-145): no attacker-controlled length reaches a copy. Will/LWT copies go through try_strdup (strlen-bounded). No independent memory-safety issue in this handler beyond D1 upstream and D12's missing connected-state guard."
