            "text": "Encode-side sizing and dispatch — Ruled out: src/mqtt.c pack_* functions, mqtt_pack dispatch, mqtt_size, mqtt_encode_length\n\nruled_out for the dispatch and size math (note fb95db R3): mqtt_pack (mqtt.c:529-535) only ever receives server-built packets (CONNACK_B, SUBACK_B, PUBLISH_B from mqtt_packet_publish/PUBLISH_B literals, PINGRESP_B, explicit mqtt_pack_mono bytes) — no decoded header byte reaches pack_handlers[], so the pack_handlers[13] array cannot be indexed out of range. mqtt_size (mqtt.c:640-674) arithmetic cannot wrap for the 512KB max_request_size (usize, additions only). The one real write hazard in this family is the caller-side wbuf accumulation, tracked separately (handlers.c publish_message / subscribe_handler)."
