            "text": "Iterator invalidation / dangling pointers during container mutation — Ruled out: remove-while-iterating in list.c/list.h, subscriber.c, iterator.c and client_deactivate's subscription teardown\n\nNamed control: every teardown path mutates a different container than the one being iterated. client_deactivate and read_callback iterate session->subscriptions with list_foreach (list.h:84-86) and call topic_del_subscriber, which operates on t->subscribers (uthash) in topic.c:107-115; the list nodes themselves are untouched, and list_remove (list.h:93-112, the only mutating iteration) is used solely for store->wildcards outside any foreach. publish_message's HASH_ITER over t->subscribers (handlers.c:136-243) only adds to s->outgoing_msgs, never deletes subscriber entries. No topic is destroyed at runtime (topic_store_del/trie_delete have no callers), so no destructor runs under an iterator."
          },
