            "text": "Config-value overflow / misparse and insecure defaults — Ruled out: src/config.c parsing (string values, numeric sizes, password_file, allow_anonymous, tls_protocols, defaults)\n\nNamed control for attacker reachability: every value passed to add_config_value comes from config_load reading an operator-owned file (-c argument or DEFAULT_CONF_PATH) or from sol.c getopt; no network input reaches this parser, so the strcpy overflow into config.port/hostname (config.c:219-253), the unbounded ':'/'\\n' scan in config_read_passwd_file (config.c:457-462) and the unchecked size multipliers (config.c:64-111) are operator-triggered only. The insecure *defaults* (allow_anonymous true at config.c:368, 50MB max_request_size and TLS 1.0/1.1 in conf/sol.conf) are recorded separately as posture issues."
