          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/retained-message-ownership-replacement-and-unbounded-growth",
          "ruleIndex": 31,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Retained-message ownership, replacement and unbounded growth — Requires further review: retained message store (struct topic.retained_msg, handlers.c:256-261 / 746-749 / 615-619)\n\nConfirmed by trace: each retained publish overwrites t->retained_msg without freeing the previous buffer (handlers.c:747) and the LWT path does the same (handlers.c:259-261); no cap on retained size or topic count; the buffer is replayed into a subscriber's fixed wbuf with only alloc_size as the length (handlers.c:615-619), which is the write-buffer overflow trigger. Owners: topic (freed only by topic_destroy, which never runs at runtime)."
          },
