        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/authentication-bypass-unauthorized-publish-and-retained-message-injection",
          "ruleIndex": 36,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Authentication bypass / unauthorized publish and retained-message injection — Requires further review: Pre-CONNECT PUBLISH against allow_anonymous=false broker (src/server.c process_message -> handlers.c publish_handler)\n\nCONFIRMED, report not filed here. No connected/authenticated gate in process_message or publish_handler. Anonymous socket PUBLISH (0x31 retain=1) accepted with no error; QoS1 publish answered `40 07 07` (PUBACK); retained payload from the anonymous socket delivered to an authenticated subscriber (`31 00 0b ... | 90 00 01 00`); anonymous retain overwrote TRUSTED-ORIGINAL with FORGED-BY-ANON for both the live subscriber and later subscribers. Control: same publish after valid CONNECT behaves identically. PoC /workspace/poc/poc_preauth_publish.py, evidence /workspace/poc/evidence/02_preauth_authz.txt."
          },
          "locations": [
