        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unbounded-memory-growth-remote-resource-exhaustion-dos",
          "ruleIndex": 38,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded memory growth / remote resource-exhaustion DoS — Requires further review: Session teardown for clean_session=false clients (src/server.c client_deactivate, lines 411-451)\n\nCONFIRMED, report not filed here. client_deactivate (server.c:430-443) frees the client/session only when clean_session==true. Measured on the dev build (max_request_size 1MB): 40 cycles clean_session=1 plateau at +6156 KiB total (0 KiB/cycle from cycle ~15); 40 cycles clean_session=0 with unique ClientId grow +155664 KiB = 3891.6 KiB/connection, linear (VmRSS 54 MB -> 210 MB). Decomposition: same ClientId + DISCONNECT = 2048-2253 KiB/cycle (the two max_request_size buffers), so the per-session tables (i_acks 512 KiB + i_msgs ~1.5 MiB) add ~1.6 MiB. Under RLIMIT_AS=700MB the broker exits after 127 connections: \"memory.c:51 Out of memory (1048576 bytes)\", status 1. PoC /workspace/poc/poc_session_leak.py, evidence /workspace/poc/evidence/04_session_leak.txt."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Session teardown for clean_session=false clients (src/server.c client_deactivate, lines 411-451)"
                }
              ]
            }
