        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/u16-counter-underflow-permanently-satisfying-has-inflight",
          "ruleIndex": 39,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "u16 counter underflow permanently satisfying has_inflight() — Ruled out: client_session.inflights counter (src/sol_internal.h:231, handlers.c:796/850)\n\nNo separate defect. Both decrement sites (handlers.c:796, :850) are preceded by inflight_msg_clear; a NULL i_msgs[id].packet crashes the handler before the decrement (proven), and a non-NULL one is only written by publish_message (handlers.c:204/218) which increments inflights next to inflight_msg_init, so the counter is >=1. Reusing an in-flight mid needs next_free_mid (handlers.c:118-121) to wrap at 65536. No reachable sequence found; the counter stayed consistent across a real QoS1 publish/ack round trip (broker healthy afterwards). Latent hardening gap at most."
          },
