        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-brute-force-no-rate-limiting-or-lockout",
          "ruleIndex": 40,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential brute force / no rate limiting or lockout — Requires further review: CONNECT authentication failure path (bad_auth, src/handlers.c:483-487) with allow_anonymous=false\n\nMeasured: 4 wrong-password CONNECTs on one socket each answered `20 00 04` with the socket kept open, then a retained PUBLISH from that never-authenticated socket was accepted and delivered to an authenticated subscriber, then a correct-password CONNECT on the same socket was accepted (`20 00 00`). No delay, lockout, connection close, or attempt counter exists in the bad_auth path (handlers.c:482-487) — only the cost of one SHA-512-crypt verification per attempt limits throughput. Supporting weakness for the auth-bypass finding; low severity on its own. Evidence /workspace/poc/evidence/02_preauth_authz.txt."
          },
