            "text": "Credential brute force / missing rate limiting — Requires further review: Repeated CONNECT on a single socket after rc=4 (server.c process_message re-arm path)\n\nConfirmed: after rc=4 the broker neither closes the socket nor slows down. 2157 CONNECT attempts with wrong passwords on ONE TCP socket in 5.00s = 431.2 attempts/s (all rc=4), and a correct password on that same socket afterwards still returned rc=0. No lockout, backoff or disconnect exists (handlers.c returns MQTT_BAD_USERNAME_OR_PASSWORD and server.c just enqueues the CONNACK and re-arms EV_READ). Not filed as a report per task instruction; parent should decide (medium: offline-dictionary-speed online guessing per connection, scales with connection count)."
