          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Auth fail-open on missing/unreadable credential store — Ruled out: allow_anonymous=false with no/missing/empty/unreadable password_file (src/server.c:982)\n\nFour configs with allow_anonymous=false were started and probed with no credentials / any user+pass / the valid alice credential: no password_file line, password_file to a nonexistent path, empty file, and chmod 000 file. Every attempt returned CONNACK rc=4 in all four cases (fail closed). server.c logs \"Failed to read passwd file\" and continues with an empty auth table, so the only consequence is total lockout rather than open access. Control: the same probe with a valid password_file returned rc=0 for alice/secret123."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "allow_anonymous=false with no/missing/empty/unreadable password_file (src/server.c:982)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
