              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/data-race-in-credential-verification-wrong-accept-reject",
          "ruleIndex": 49,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Data race in credential verification (wrong accept/reject) — Requires further review: check_passwd()/crypt(3) under concurrent authentication (src/util.c:142, 3 event-loop threads)\n\nConfirmed false rejects, no false accepts. Library level: libcrypt 4.5.2 crypt() called from 3 threads with one salt produced 3340 wrong results out of 3352 calls (0/900 wrong serially). Broker level: serial control 60/60 good accepted and 60/60 bad rejected; with 4 concurrent clients 2063/2140 correct-password attempts got CONNACK rc=4 and 0/2138 wrong-password attempts were accepted; second run (8 workers, 90 s) 21558/22508 legit rejected, 0/22883 wrong-password accepts. Root cause: sol calls non-reentrant crypt() from 3 event loops with no lock (util.c:142-145, handlers.c). Impact is authentication DoS / lockout of a known account, not bypass. Not filed per task instruction."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "check_passwd()/crypt(3) under concurrent authentication (src/util.c:142, 3 event-loop threads)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
