              "risk_area": "Data race in credential verification (wrong accept/reject)",
              "surface": "check_passwd()/crypt(3) under concurrent authentication (src/util.c:142, 3 event-loop threads)",
              "recorded_by": "Auth and TLS Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/pre-authentication-denial-of-service-busy-loop",
          "ruleIndex": 50,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Pre-authentication denial of service (busy loop) — Requires further review: TLS data path ssl_recv_bytes() (src/network.c:438-455)\n\nConfirmed pre-auth CPU exhaustion, no credentials needed: one TLS connection that sends a 3-byte truncated record (`16 03 01`) and stays silent pins a worker thread in ssl_recv_bytes()'s `continue` on SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ. LD_PRELOAD counter on SSL_read shows ~800,000 calls/second (777451, 865766, 869275, 847659, 800826, 789077, 719399, 898729). One connection = 74-86% of a core; 3 connections (one per event loop, THREADSNR=2+main) = ~200% CPU with per-thread ticks 857/790/969, and a legitimate TLS client then cannot complete a handshake (8 s timeout). Not filed per task instruction; this is the highest-impact item found (A:H, AV:N, PR:N)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "TLS data path ssl_recv_bytes() (src/network.c:438-455)"
                }
              ]
