              "surface": "TLS data path ssl_recv_bytes() (src/network.c:438-455)",
              "recorded_by": "Auth and TLS Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/weak-tls-protocol-versions-enabled-by-shipped-configuration",
          "ruleIndex": 51,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Weak TLS protocol versions enabled by shipped configuration — Requires further review: tls_protocols policy (src/config.c:191-265, conf/sol.conf) and protocol negotiation\n\nObserved with openssl s_client against a broker using the shipped protocol list: TLSv1 ACCEPTED (ECDHE-RSA-AES256-SHA), TLSv1.1 ACCEPTED, TLSv1.2 and TLSv1.3 ACCEPTED; TLSv1.0 succeeded even at s_client's default security level, so the server really offers it. `tls_protocols tlsv1_2` correctly rejected 1.0/1.1/1.3. Default when the directive is omitted is TLSv1.2 only (TLSv1.3 rejected because `#ifdef TLS1_3_VERSION` is false while compiling config.h). Weak/insecure default rather than an exploitable flaw; not filed per task instruction."
          },
          "locations": [
