            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/memory-exhaustion-denial-of-service-per-connection-buffer-cost",
          "ruleIndex": 53,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Memory exhaustion denial of service (per-connection buffer cost) — Requires further review: max_request_size buffer allocation per client (src/server.c:client_init, shipped conf 50MB)\n\nConfirmed: try_calloc is malloc+memset so both per-client buffers are resident immediately. With `max_request_size 50MB` 20 idle TCP connections (no bytes, no credentials) took RSS from 76 MB to 2145 MB = ~107 MB/connection, retained after all closed; with 1MB the same test is ~2 MB/connection. max_memory is never enforced and try_alloc exits on failure (memory.c:49-53): under an 800 MB address-space cap the broker died at the 8th connection, \"Out of memory (52428800 bytes)\", exit status 1. Not filed per task instruction; availability impact for the shipped 50MB config."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
