              "recorded_by": "Auth and TLS Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/processing-of-mqtt-commands-by-an-unauthenticated-peer-crash",
          "ruleIndex": 54,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Processing of MQTT commands by an unauthenticated peer (crash) — Requires further review: Rejected CONNECT followed by SUBSCRIBE on the same socket (handlers.c:588 subscriber_new)\n\nConfirmed with the ASan build: CONNECT with a wrong password returns CONNACK rc=4, then the same socket can send SUBSCRIBE and the broker dispatches it - subscriber_new (src/subscriber.c:45) dereferences a NULL client_session (\"runtime error: member access within null pointer of type 'struct client_session'\") and the broker aborts. Two small packets, no credentials, pre-auth denial of service. This sits on the boundary with the pre-CONNECT/dispatch area another agent owns, so it is recorded here for the parent to route/dedupe rather than filed."
          },
