        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/insecure-shipped-defaults-no-auth-legacy-tls-oversized-buffers",
          "ruleIndex": 55,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Insecure shipped defaults (no auth, legacy TLS, oversized buffers) — Requires further review: Shipped conf/sol.conf security posture\n\nConfirmed posture, three parts: (1) allow_anonymous is commented out in conf/sol.conf and the compiled default is true, so the shipped deployment is unauthenticated; (2) the shipped tls_protocols value enables TLS 1.0 and 1.1 (verified accepted) alongside 1.2/1.3; (3) max_request_size 50MB costs ~107 MB RSS per idle connection and exhaustion kills the process. The broker also refuses to start as shipped because certs/ca.crt is absent (fail-closed, exit 1), so the TLS defaults only apply once an operator supplies certificates. Recorded as an insecure-default observation, not an exploitable flaw."
          },
          "locations": [
