        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-string-confusion-embedded-nul",
          "ruleIndex": 56,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential string confusion (embedded NUL) — Requires further review: Embedded NUL bytes in CONNECT username/password (unpack_string16, mqtt.c:251-257)\n\nConfirmed: username `alice\\0junk` with the correct password returned rc=0 (C-string truncation in the uthash lookup), and passwords `secret123\\0junk` / `secret123\\0` also returned rc=0 (crypt stops at NUL). MQTT 3.1.1 requires UTF-8 strings without U+0000, which sol never validates. Low on its own - the same credential is reached by a shorter string - but it is a second credential representation that any auditing/provisioning component would treat differently."
          },
          "locations": [
