        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/blocking-handshake-slowloris-on-the-accept-path",
          "ruleIndex": 57,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Blocking handshake / slowloris on the accept path — Ruled out: TLS handshake at accept time (conn_tls_accept / ssl_accept, network.c:393-401,500-510)\n\nCandidate was \"a blocking SSL_accept in the accept path stalls the listener\". Disproved: accept_conn() sets the client socket non-blocking (network.c:211) and ssl_accept() is attempted once, so an idle TLS connection that sends nothing consumes 0 CPU ticks over 2 s and any subsequent byte causes SSL_read to fail hard and the connection to be closed (\"Closing connection ... : Success\"). A legitimate TLS client was still served (CONNACK 20 02 00 00 in 0.01 s) while an idle socket was held. The real spin needs a byte to arrive first, which is covered by the ssl_recv_bytes entry."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "TLS handshake at accept time (conn_tls_accept / ssl_accept, network.c:393-401,500-510)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Blocking handshake / slowloris on the accept path",
              "surface": "TLS handshake at accept time (conn_tls_accept / ssl_accept, network.c:393-401,500-510)",
              "recorded_by": "Auth and TLS Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/control-flow-hijack-via-overwritten-function-pointer-in-the-decoded-packet-refcount-free-indirect-call",
          "ruleIndex": 58,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Control-flow hijack via overwritten function pointer in the decoded packet (refcount.free indirect call) — Ruled out: CONNECT ClientId overflow, control-flow variant (mqtt.c:235-243 memcpy into client_id[64] inside struct io_event, mqtt.c:568-598 mqtt_packet_destroy)\n\ngdb at connect_handler with cid_len=102 shows username/password/will_topic/will_message holding 0x41../0x42../0x43../0x44.. inside the 144-byte `io` frame. Control that rules the control-flow variant out: mqtt_packet_destroy's CONNECT branch frees only those four pointers and never touches refcount; each free is gated on a flag bit located before the copied region, and with those bits set unpack_mqtt_connect rewrites the pointers with fresh heap allocations (observed 0x7f9d.. values with flags=0xc6); no code path DECREFs a decoded packet (DECREF only on mqtt_packet_alloc copies, handlers.c:755, and i_msgs, handlers.c:93). Aiming refcount.free at 0xdeadbeefcafebabe (cid_len=110) then CONNECT/PINGREQ/PUBLISH/DISCONNECT/close left the broker alive. ASan-only build: silent for cid_len<=117 (overflow stays inside io), reports WRITE of size 1 at mqtt.c:241 for 118 and WRITE of size 130 at mqtt.c:240 for 130. No stack protector: no __stack_chk_fail/__stack_chk_guard and zero fs:0x28 loads in both harness binaries. PoC /workspace/poc/poc_cid_refcount.py; note fd300c."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "CONNECT ClientId overflow, control-flow variant (mqtt.c:235-243 memcpy into client_id[64] inside struct io_event, mqtt.c:568-598 mqtt_packet_destroy)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Control-flow hijack via overwritten function pointer in the decoded packet (refcount.free indirect call)",
              "surface": "CONNECT ClientId overflow, control-flow variant (mqtt.c:235-243 memcpy into client_id[64] inside struct io_event, mqtt.c:568-598 mqtt_packet_destroy)",
              "recorded_by": "Decoder Secondary Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        }
